WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.499 --> 00:00:02.970
PRIYANKA VERGADIA: Welcome
to Deconstructing Chatbots.

00:00:02.970 --> 00:00:05.710
I am Priyanka Vergadia,
and in this episode,

00:00:05.710 --> 00:00:09.080
we are going to build
our first chatbot.

00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:11.930
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:17.540
Like a promise, we are
going to jump right

00:00:17.540 --> 00:00:20.450
into the Dialogflow interface.

00:00:20.450 --> 00:00:24.110
Navigate to console to
Dialogflow.com and sign in.

00:00:24.110 --> 00:00:26.450
If you're a first time user,
then just use your email

00:00:26.450 --> 00:00:27.530
to sign up.

00:00:27.530 --> 00:00:29.150
Accept all the terms
and conditions,

00:00:29.150 --> 00:00:31.140
and you'll be in the console.

00:00:31.140 --> 00:00:33.140
Now, create new agent.

00:00:33.140 --> 00:00:35.760
Let's call this
appointment scheduler.

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:38.360
Dialogflow creates a
GCP project for you

00:00:38.360 --> 00:00:40.730
to access logs and
Cloud functions.

00:00:40.730 --> 00:00:43.190
You can select an
existing project as well.

00:00:43.190 --> 00:00:45.110
Then, just create.

00:00:45.110 --> 00:00:49.040
You get two default intents
as a part of your agent.

00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:52.580
The default welcome intent
helps greet your users.

00:00:52.580 --> 00:00:56.300
And the default fallback intent
helps catch all the questions

00:00:56.300 --> 00:00:58.460
that your bot does
not understand.

00:00:58.460 --> 00:01:01.160
At this point, you
have a functional bot.

00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:03.650
All it does is greet the users.

00:01:03.650 --> 00:01:05.600
Well, let's test it.

00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:08.000
If we say hi, our
bot responds back

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:11.580
with a hi, and a how
I can help message.

00:01:11.580 --> 00:01:15.290
Once you ask for help, such
as, set an appointment,

00:01:15.290 --> 00:01:16.800
it does not know what to do.

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:19.010
So it kicks in the
fallback intent,

00:01:19.010 --> 00:01:21.470
obviously because we've
not created any intent

00:01:21.470 --> 00:01:23.780
to catch that
particular request.

00:01:23.780 --> 00:01:25.730
So let's add that now.

00:01:25.730 --> 00:01:31.950
Let's create a new intent and
call it schedule appointment.

00:01:31.950 --> 00:01:34.710
We will skip context
and events for now.

00:01:34.710 --> 00:01:36.720
Let's get down to
the training phrases

00:01:36.720 --> 00:01:39.180
and add some phrases here.

00:01:39.180 --> 00:01:41.040
As you're putting
these in, you will

00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:44.220
see date and time are
automatically identified

00:01:44.220 --> 00:01:48.380
as system entity date and time.

00:01:48.380 --> 00:01:50.840
Now, to make this
functional, we need

00:01:50.840 --> 00:01:52.890
to respond back to the user.

00:01:52.890 --> 00:01:54.620
So let's add a response.

00:01:54.620 --> 00:01:57.440
You could just say, you're
all set, see you then.

00:01:57.440 --> 00:02:00.800
Or you could make it a little
bit more interesting and say,

00:02:00.800 --> 00:02:04.500
you're all set for this
date and this time.

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:05.390
See you then.

00:02:05.390 --> 00:02:12.240
The dollar sign here helps
you access the entity values.

00:02:12.240 --> 00:02:15.000
Let's test it with, set
an appointment for 4:00

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:17.220
PM on Thursday.

00:02:17.220 --> 00:02:19.710
And as expected, you
get the right response

00:02:19.710 --> 00:02:23.560
with the right date and time.

00:02:23.560 --> 00:02:27.490
Now, what if somebody just
said, set an appointment?

00:02:27.490 --> 00:02:29.800
Well, that is not
really specific,

00:02:29.800 --> 00:02:33.250
and we have not yet handled
that scenario in our bot.

00:02:33.250 --> 00:02:37.270
To support this, we use
something called slot filling.

00:02:37.270 --> 00:02:40.240
We make the entities
as required,

00:02:40.240 --> 00:02:44.920
and Dialogflow will make sure
to ask for both date and time

00:02:44.920 --> 00:02:46.930
before it responds back.

00:02:46.930 --> 00:02:48.970
Let's add, what
time would you like

00:02:48.970 --> 00:02:52.480
to come in, for the time
prompt, and what date,

00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:54.340
for the date prompt.

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:58.220
You can add other variants,
too, and then just save.

00:02:58.220 --> 00:03:02.730
OK, let's test one more time
to see if things are working.

00:03:02.730 --> 00:03:05.190
Let's say, set an appointment.

00:03:05.190 --> 00:03:08.630
Our bot responds with, what
time would you like to come in?

00:03:08.630 --> 00:03:10.280
And I say, 10:00 AM.

00:03:10.280 --> 00:03:14.400
And then it asks for the
date, and I say February 12.

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:16.190
All right, got all that.

00:03:16.190 --> 00:03:17.750
It's all working.

00:03:17.750 --> 00:03:22.670
OK, so all the testing we did so
far has been in the simulator.

00:03:22.670 --> 00:03:26.090
But what if you wanted to
share this win with a friend?

00:03:26.090 --> 00:03:30.320
Let's go into integration
and enable the web demo.

00:03:30.320 --> 00:03:33.500
And just like that, you
have a link to your bot

00:03:33.500 --> 00:03:36.920
that you can share or a
iFrame into your website

00:03:36.920 --> 00:03:38.960
or mobile application.

00:03:38.960 --> 00:03:40.650
You can test to see
if it's working.

00:03:48.980 --> 00:03:52.950
All right, so today we set up
a simple appointment scheduler

00:03:52.950 --> 00:03:56.760
that takes date and
time as input variables,

00:03:56.760 --> 00:03:59.520
and responds back to the
user with an appointment

00:03:59.520 --> 00:04:01.110
confirmation.

00:04:01.110 --> 00:04:03.780
We also learned
about slot filling.

00:04:03.780 --> 00:04:08.550
If a user only provided us with
a date, or time, or nothing,

00:04:08.550 --> 00:04:12.330
how you can prompt the user to
provide the missing information

00:04:12.330 --> 00:04:13.800
seamlessly.

00:04:13.800 --> 00:04:17.070
And finally, we learned how to
test our bot in the simulator

00:04:17.070 --> 00:04:19.709
and integrated it
into a website.

00:04:19.709 --> 00:04:22.650
Don't miss the next episode
of Deconstructing Chatbots

00:04:22.650 --> 00:04:24.750
because we are going
to make our appointment

00:04:24.750 --> 00:04:26.790
scheduler a little bit smarter.

00:04:26.790 --> 00:04:30.140
[MUSIC PLAYING]

